# Privacy

Product code makes **no new outbound network calls**. The CLI, `enact ui`, generated reports, and the Pages app talk only to the machine they run on (ADR 0007, ADR 0014).

- Servers bind `127.0.0.1`.
- The hosted Pages app evaluates in the tab. It does not accept uploads.
- Same-origin fetch of vendored `policy.wasm` is allowed. CDNs for the engine, SDK, fonts, or analytics are not.
- Adapters (`enact-adapt`) are file-in / file-out. No cloud SDKs and no outbound calls from `src/enact/`.
- A new third-party call (CDN, telemetry, hosted API) needs a new ADR that explicitly allows it. Otherwise reject the change.
- **AI keys are never written** into source, fixtures, reports, HTML, env samples, or logs.

See `docs/adr/0007-local-only-privacy-model.md` and `docs/adr/0014-browser-app-is-primary.md`.
